RhxE","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-06T21:50:53Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T21:50:53Z","body":"No, the CI fails in code unrelated to your changes, see diff:\r\n<img width=\"767\" height=\"211\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3e475384-fa4a-42f6-99de-fdd6a61beda1\" />\r\n\r\nNo clue why this starts failing now and not before... Does the linter cache files, and maybe a rule was updated without invalidating cache?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4014349380/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4014410608","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117160#issuecomment-4014410608","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117160","id":4014410608,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vRwtw","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-06T22:04:46Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T22:04:46Z","body":"> Hi @Bromeon, GDScript already has this via `@GlobalScope.type_string` method, as it is exposed there via the Variant Utility Functions contracts.\r\n\r\nBut [`type_string`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_@globalscope.html#class-globalscope-method-type-string) does the opposite? :thinking: \r\n```gdscript\r\nString type_string(type: int)\r\n```\r\nwhereas this converts `GDExtensionConstStringPtr` to `GDExtensionVariantType`...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4014410608/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4014564921","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117160#issuecomment-4014564921","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117160","id":4014564921,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vSWY5","user":{"login":"Naros","id":3255568,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTU1Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3255568?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros","html_url":"https://github.com/Naros","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-06T22:45:13Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T22:45:42Z","body":"Oh, you're right, I completely got it reversed. I can add a GlobalScope equivalent, but I guess the question is what would be a good name for it?  I believe something like `Variant::Type type(name: String)` might be a bit too vague? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4014564921/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4015895512","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117160#issuecomment-4015895512","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117160","id":4015895512,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vXbPY","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-07T07:57:30Z","updated_at":"2026-03-07T07:57:30Z","body":"In my opinion, we should focus on a unified API rather than adding methods for specific enums on a case-by-case basis. There's already an API for `ClassDB` and, to some extent, for `Script`. The problem is that there's no public API for global constants and enums.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4015895512/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4016668971","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117160#issuecomment-4016668971","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117160","id":4016668971,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vaYEr","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-07T15:06:30Z","updated_at":"2026-03-07T15:06:30Z","body":"Personally, I think adding this function to the GDExtension interface is fine. We already have `variant_get_type_name`, this would just be adding its partner function to do the reverse. I don't think we need block this in favor of solving this issue for GDScript or all enums in general.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4016668971/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4075777887","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117160#issuecomment-4075777887","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117160","id":4075777887,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7y729f","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T15:17:07Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T15:17:07Z","body":"This is failing a clang-tidy test on CI, but it's about code that this PR doesn't change. Perhaps this needs a rebase to catch a fix that's already in `master`?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4075777887/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4080896929","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117160#issuecomment-4080896929","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117160","id":4080896929,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zPYuh","user":{"login":"Naros","id":3255568,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTU1Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3255568?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros","html_url":"https://github.com/Naros","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-18T09:10:07Z","updated_at":"2026-03-18T09:10:07Z","body":"@dsnopek rebased, let's see how CI fairs.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4080896929/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4166254107","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117160#issuecomment-4166254107","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117160","id":4166254107,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74U_4b","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T23:13:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T23:13:27Z","body":"We discussed this at today's GDExtension team meeting, and a lot of good points were raised.\r\n\r\nWe generally agreed that having a generic system for translating enum values to/from names is a good idea. But, that it would need to be two systems for now: one of object enums and another for variant enums (pre unification via GDType). But, also, that wouldn't fully solve the problem here, since the strings in question _aren't_ the enum names, but the type names used in places such as the docs XML (so, `Vector2i`, `StringName` and `bool`, not `TYPE_VECTOR2I`, `TYPE_STRING_NAME` and `TYPE_BOOL`). So, we'd still need something else to convert these particular strings to ints.\r\n\r\nHaving each language binding have their own translation table is a workable solution. If we did that, we could deprecate the existing `variant_get_type_name`, and then the GDExtension interface is a little smaller.\r\n\r\nHowever, the overall consensus among the folks in attendance, is that this is something that multiple people have asked for, and the implementation is very simple (it's adding a 4 line function), and so \"why not\" add it :-)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4166254107/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4224911575","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117160#issuecomment-4224911575","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117160","id":4224911575,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc770wjX","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/use